# DHIS2 Docker image pins per minor.
#
# Single source of truth for which exact patch we run + capture codegen against.
# The default `dhis2/core:43` tag floats — DHIS2 retags it on every patch
# release — which means committed manifests + dumps drift across time even
# without our intent. Pinning to specific tags here makes every codegen run
# reproducible: identical Docker bytes today, tomorrow, and in CI.
#
# Bumping any value here is an explicit action: `make dhis2-versions-bump`
# rewrites the non-held pins, then re-run codegen (`make dhis2-codegen-all
# VERSIONS="vN ..."`) and commit the regen in the same PR. The snapshot test
# in packages/dhis2w-codegen/tests/ then locks the new tree byte-for-byte.
#
# Image tag list: https://hub.docker.com/r/dhis2/core/tags
#
# A pin is a `dhis2/core` tag, or a full image reference for a major that has
# no release yet. v44 is a preview pinned to one build of the development line
# (`dhis2/core-dev:master`, 2.44-SNAPSHOT revision c48aedc, built 2026-10-06) by
# digest, so it cannot move underneath the committed codegen and dump. It is
# held; re-pin it to `2.44.0.0` when 2.44.0 is released.

# 2.41.9.x reported no `mapView` schema on /api/schemas (BUGS.md #43); 2.41.10.0 lists it again,
# so the generated v41 tree carries MapView once more. `dhis2w_client.v{N}.maps` keeps the
# hand-written MapView and enums so the three trees expose one shape regardless of the schema.
DHIS2_V41=2.41.10.0
DHIS2_V42=2.42.6.0
DHIS2_V43=2.43.2.0
DHIS2_V44=dhis2/core-dev@sha256:4807b0252211282642eb1f13455f79e6196358534a1fd94ed083a5008ce0e926 # held
